dependent node1-node2 links (active use of both links, not just failover-capable)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1/node2 were bonded (bond0, balance-rr mode, confirmed via /proc/net/bonding/bond0 showing 'load balancing (round-robin)' with both eth1/eth2 slaves MII up) carrying a routed path between 172.31.13.0/24 (node3 side) and 172.31.24.0/24 (node4 side). A 40-packet ping burst from node3 to node4 showed simultaneous TX counter increments of ~20 packets on both eth1 and eth2 on node1 (122->142, 117->137), directly demonstrating both physical links carrying traffic concurrently rather than one idle standby link.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bb4b68c2630a42ff\",\"cmd-59636f10ed1344ce\",\"cmd-474a5911f52241ef\",\"cmd-cf20ade7c78f40c7\",\"cmd-d30ab92ed977444f\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"node3 and node4 keep reaching each other when link1 (node1.eth1<->node2.eth1) is taken out of service, and traffic resumes over both links after it is restored\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"With a continuous ping running from node3 to node4, eth1 was taken down symmetrically on both node1 and node2; bond0 on both nodes showed the eth1 slave go MII down while eth2 kept the bond up. The ping log during the outage recorded 79 uninterrupted successful replies (seq 66-85 shown, no gaps), i.e. 0% loss. After eth1 was brought back up, bond0 showed both slaves MII up again and TX counters on both eth1/eth2 incremented, confirming traffic resumed over both links.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3fbfe0b2747e4e7a\",\"cmd-f30bafd69edc41d6\",\"cmd-d45f695e2e004b3c\",\"cmd-18e4b42780754978\",\"cmd-4906e240925640c5\",\"cmd-664c761d3f7c4b35\",\"cmd-170f690988ed4559\",\"cmd-282ce88c58144800\",\"cmd-cb87ecc0b3284efa\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"node3 and node4 keep reaching each other when link2 (node1.eth2<->node2.eth2) is taken out of service, and traffic resumes over both links after it is restored\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Repeating the same test with eth2 taken down symmetrically on both nodes while a continuous ping ran, the ping log recorded 79 consecutive successful replies (seq 1-79, no gaps) confirming 0% loss failover to link1. After eth2 was restored, bond0 showed both slaves MII up and a subsequent 5-ping test showed 0% loss, confirming recovery.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e296c6d487714423\",\"cmd-0420ef2b46f24460\",\"cmd-1268b82fcbad47ba\",\"cmd-67a22fb6d0134292\",\"cmd-49605b10de2a4f7c\",\"cmd-1081b4033be24ad0\",\"cmd-f047a4b0802145e5\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on all four managed nodes (independent of the public task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1, node2, node3, node4: a pre-restart boot_id and healthy-state baseline was captured, a `reboot` was issued and acknowledged, exec access was polled until it returned, a changed boot_id was confirmed, and recovered bond/interface/route/ip_forward state plus end-to-end node3<->node4 connectivity were verified. The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot independently corroborates all four post-restart boot_ids matching the executor's own captured values, and a final joint check after all four restarts showed 10/10 pings (0% loss) and both bond slaves up on both SONiC nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3f394c7364f442b4\",\"cmd-c0b73ed27e674f4c\",\"cmd-ffd6405a560a4fe2\",\"cmd-a78f87b947e64642\",\"cmd-b1f107c9e1614483\",\"cmd-9b97142f049f4cae\",\"cmd-d962250cc2b744dd\",\"cmd-1875784aa13042c9\",\"cmd-ced240c2be984163\",\"cmd-0d9b028f426c46aa\",\"cmd-2b81b10164664a4b\",\"cmd-a93b7bc40fd944f7\",\"cmd-275abc66149d4afe\",\"cmd-094109fd35b14d37\",\"cmd-df022ebcdbb64a53\",\"cmd-b05f13e8f6f94435\",\"cmd-8dd1abf4df044670\",\"cmd-fb654038de2f4c74\",\"cmd-3da00c82637c4231\",\"cmd-e178e968cae9497a\",\"cmd-ce4d5de27672429b\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_e